{
  "name": "Avoiding Common Faucet Installation Headaches",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Installing an easy grip faucet can seem straightforward, but a few common mistakes can turn it into a real headache. First off, many folks forget to properly seat that O-ring around the opening before dropping the faucet in. That's your first line of defense against leaks! Then, when you're underneath the sink, don't rush tightening that mounting nut. You want to make sure the faucet is perfectly positioned before you secure it. If it's crooked, you'll likely have issues. Another big one is using the wrong supply-line connector. Manufacturers often specify what's needed, and if your existing lines don't match, you'll run into trouble. Always make sure to flush both hot and cold water through for at least a minute after installation to clear any debris and, crucially, to check for any hidden leaks. Skipping that final leak check is just asking for a surprise puddle later! If you find yourself in a bind, maybe the access under your sink is super tight, or you just can't get those connections sealed, don't hesitate to reach out to a professional. HH Remodeling LLC is always happy to lend a hand with those trickier installations around Denver and surrounding communities.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
